    {
      "id": "j3LTusCmTwmq6mTLCDltl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.33228207433376,
      "y": -1160.0042453079,
      "width": 1663.199951171875,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 390581429,
      "version": 358,
      "versionNonce": 657591780,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We are used to monitoring workload on Kubernetes, so we can easily look at metrics\nlike CPU usage, memory usage, throughput (the number of requests per second), and\nlatency (the time to process a request). The same approach applies to LLMs, but with\nimportant differences.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We are used to monitoring workload on Kubernetes, so we can easily look at metrics\nlike CPU usage, memory usage, throughput (the number of requests per second), and\nlatency (the time to process a request). The same approach applies to LLMs, but with\nimportant differences.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wfXzYLUFYeDJiLRf1JRQA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120.33228207433376,
      "y": -1260.0042453079,
      "width": 2673,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 645295637,
      "version": 331,
      "versionNonce": 657011292,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "file:///home/aaiche/Documents/00-Delivery/82-AI267-v2.25/cl-oreilly-generative-ai-kubernetes-analyst-material-3188555kr-202603-en_0.pdf",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "file:///home/aaiche/Documents/00-Delivery/82-AI267-v2.25/cl-oreilly-generative-ai-kubernetes-analyst-material-3188555kr-202603-en_0.pdf",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bLHaRbFR9uRhg3l9mVkuI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.33228207433376,
      "y": -760.0042453079,
      "width": 1603.800048828125,
      "height": 135,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 235529077,
      "version": 311,
      "versionNonce": 553562468,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " two main phases of LLM inference execution, prefill and decode, are very\ndifferent because the first is compute-bound while the second is memory-bound. We\ncovered these phases in “Understanding LLM Fundamentals” on page xxvii.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " two main phases of LLM inference execution, prefill and decode, are very\ndifferent because the first is compute-bound while the second is memory-bound. We\ncovered these phases in “Understanding LLM Fundamentals” on page xxvii.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pUhGWGHO_wD6zl4dXT3T6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.33228207433376,
      "y": -500.00424530789996,
      "width": 1683,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 306687189,
      "version": 315,
      "versionNonce": 2022344412,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The problem is not limited to resource usage. Even the concept of throughput or\nlatency is different because it is not possible to predict, given a request, how long\nthe answer will be, so any metric that counts the requests will not provide a good\nrepresentation of the actual model server workload\n\nSince tokens are the core unit of computation for LLM generation, model server\nmetrics are token-based rather than request-base",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The problem is not limited to resource usage. Even the concept of throughput or\nlatency is different because it is not possible to predict, given a request, how long\nthe answer will be, so any metric that counts the requests will not provide a good\nrepresentation of the actual model server workload\n\nSince tokens are the core unit of computation for LLM generation, model server\nmetrics are token-based rather than request-base",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XJeWxwDYyU71Vk02lhq8i",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120.33228207433376,
      "y": 79.99575469209822,
      "width": 1762.199951171875,
      "height": 585,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1388661301,
      "version": 317,
      "versionNonce": 275440868,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Time To First Token:\nTime To First Token (TTFT) is the actual time that a user waits before starting to\nreceive the response.\nThis is the most important metric for real-time use cases like chatbots, but it is less\ncritical for offline scenarios like batch jobs where users don’t experience the wait time\ndirectly.\nTTFT uses seconds as the unit of time and is exposed as a histogram metric type\n(which tracks the distribution of values across configurable buckets). For example, vLLM\nproduces this metric with the name vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds\n\nConsidering how LLMs work, the time to produce the first token represents the time\nnecessary to compute the prefill phase\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Time To First Token:\nTime To First Token (TTFT) is the actual time that a user waits before starting to\nreceive the response.\nThis is the most important metric for real-time use cases like chatbots, but it is less\ncritical for offline scenarios like batch jobs where users don’t experience the wait time\ndirectly.\nTTFT uses seconds as the unit of time and is exposed as a histogram metric type\n(which tracks the distribution of values across configurable buckets). For example, vLLM\nproduces this metric with the name vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds\n\nConsidering how LLMs work, the time to produce the first token represents the time\nnecessary to compute the prefill phase\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Owtw5rdugikdtOmgSvqbi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.33228207433376,
      "y": 819.9957546920982,
      "width": 1742.4000244140625,
      "height": 765,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1617443733,
      "version": 285,
      "versionNonce": 734874460,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Time Per Output Token or Inter-Token Latency :\nTokens are produced one by one and are usually returned to the user as a stream,\nso the second metric to look at is the time necessary to produce each token after the\nfirst.\nIf TTFT is the actual time the user will perceive as waiting time, Time Per Output\nToken (TPOT) represents the speed of the result as seen by the end user. This metric\nis more important for real-time use cases and less critical for offline scenarios. It is\nalso often called Inter-Token Latency (ITL).\nOn average, a human reads about 180 words per minute, or roughly 3 words per\nsecond. Since tokens approximate but don’t exactly match words, producing at least\nfour or five tokens per second ensures that humans can consume the output without\nperceived delay.\nSimilar to TTFT, this metric is computed in seconds and uses a histogram as its type.\nIn vLLM, it is named vllm:time_per_output_token_seconds,\n\nIf TTFT maps to the prefill phase, this metric measures the duration of each decoding\niteration.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Time Per Output Token or Inter-Token Latency :\nTokens are produced one by one and are usually returned to the user as a stream,\nso the second metric to look at is the time necessary to produce each token after the\nfirst.\nIf TTFT is the actual time the user will perceive as waiting time, Time Per Output\nToken (TPOT) represents the speed of the result as seen by the end user. This metric\nis more important for real-time use cases and less critical for offline scenarios. It is\nalso often called Inter-Token Latency (ITL).\nOn average, a human reads about 180 words per minute, or roughly 3 words per\nsecond. Since tokens approximate but don’t exactly match words, producing at least\nfour or five tokens per second ensures that humans can consume the output without\nperceived delay.\nSimilar to TTFT, this metric is computed in seconds and uses a histogram as its type.\nIn vLLM, it is named vllm:time_per_output_token_seconds,\n\nIf TTFT maps to the prefill phase, this metric measures the duration of each decoding\niteration.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "toMp5EYTb2MFSDWbmq1UE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 180.33228207433376,
      "y": 1799.9957546920982,
      "width": 237.60000610351562,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HswhlbVGf5qBaNZcqL3F4",
        "c7SoXNGlR-7Sh15uBS33w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 325452021,
      "version": 284,
      "versionNonce": 990160996,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706445017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Throughput :\n\n\n....\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Throughput :\n\n\n....\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000221189,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_S6yuYMCqzmJr0PRC4cXb",
