    {
      "id": "BhLcm3c4dvrL_VnvyHmpn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 100480,
      "width": 5513.2001953125,
      "height": 1330,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "ZDraw8rHnVgyMEMUn_PRD",
        "sNBEjHfnOg6Of_vys7Xe8",
        "2qW8HK9-n3fA-GxGXJGpc"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1C1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1264926453,
      "version": 161,
      "versionNonce": 2040440341,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793000731781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[student@workstation monitoring-performance]$ ./request_inference_to_qwen3.sh 3 10\nSending 3 inference requests to https://qwen3-06b-monitoring-performance.apps.lab.example.com/v1/chat/completions\nInterval: 10s between requests (CPU model, be patient)\n\nRequest 1/3 - \"What is Kubernetes?\"\n  -> Kubernetes is a **container orchestration platform** that automates the deployment, scaling, and management of containerized applications. It provides a standardized way to manage and orchestrate multiple containers across different environments. Here's a concise explanation:\n\n### What is Kubernetes?\nKubernetes is a tool that helps developers and DevOps engineers manage and scale containerized applications. It works with orchestration tools like Docker, which runs containers, and provides a consistent, scalable, and reliable way to manage these containers across multiple machines.\n\n### Key Features of Kubernetes:\n- **Orchestration**: Automates the distribution of containers across nodes.\n- **Deployment**: Manages the lifecycle of applications (up, down, scale).\n- **Scaling**: Automatically adjusts the number of containers\n\n\n\nRequest 2/3 - \"Explain containers in one sentence.\"\n  -> Containers are structured data types used in programming to hold collections of related items, such as values, and to provide a way to manage and access these items efficiently.\n\n\n\nRequest 3/3 - \"What is OpenShift?\"\n  -> OpenShift is a cloud-native open source application management platform developed by Google. It provides a centralized way to manage applications, deployments, and containers across multiple environments. OpenShift is designed to work with containers and orchestration tools, allowing developers to manage their applications more efficiently and easily.\n\nIt is often used in cloud environments like Google Cloud, AWS, and Azure. OpenShift provides features such as:\n\n- A centralized control plane\n- Application deployment and scaling\n- Support for container orchestration (e.g., Kubernetes)\n- Integration with other Google services\n- Easy access to cloud resources\n\nIt's commonly used by developers and DevOps teams to manage their applications and infrastructure in a cloud-native way.\n\n\nDone. Check the vLLM Grafana dashboard for updated metrics.\nSelect 'qwen3-06b' in the model_name dropdown.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[student@workstation monitoring-performance]$ ./request_inference_to_qwen3.sh 3 10\nSending 3 inference requests to https://qwen3-06b-monitoring-performance.apps.lab.example.com/v1/chat/completions\nInterval: 10s between requests (CPU model, be patient)\n\nRequest 1/3 - \"What is Kubernetes?\"\n  -> Kubernetes is a **container orchestration platform** that automates the deployment, scaling, and management of containerized applications. It provides a standardized way to manage and orchestrate multiple containers across different environments. Here's a concise explanation:\n\n### What is Kubernetes?\nKubernetes is a tool that helps developers and DevOps engineers manage and scale containerized applications. It works with orchestration tools like Docker, which runs containers, and provides a consistent, scalable, and reliable way to manage these containers across multiple machines.\n\n### Key Features of Kubernetes:\n- **Orchestration**: Automates the distribution of containers across nodes.\n- **Deployment**: Manages the lifecycle of applications (up, down, scale).\n- **Scaling**: Automatically adjusts the number of containers\n\n\n\nRequest 2/3 - \"Explain containers in one sentence.\"\n  -> Containers are structured data types used in programming to hold collections of related items, such as values, and to provide a way to manage and access these items efficiently.\n\n\n\nRequest 3/3 - \"What is OpenShift?\"\n  -> OpenShift is a cloud-native open source application management platform developed by Google. It provides a centralized way to manage applications, deployments, and containers across multiple environments. OpenShift is designed to work with containers and orchestration tools, allowing developers to manage their applications more efficiently and easily.\n\nIt is often used in cloud environments like Google Cloud, AWS, and Azure. OpenShift provides features such as:\n\n- A centralized control plane\n- Application deployment and scaling\n- Support for container orchestration (e.g., Kubernetes)\n- Integration with other Google services\n- Easy access to cloud resources\n\nIt's commonly used by developers and DevOps teams to manage their applications and infrastructure in a cloud-native way.\n\n\nDone. Check the vLLM Grafana dashboard for updated metrics.\nSelect 'qwen3-06b' in the model_name dropdown.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793000725891,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
